{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.sh; cat src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh; sed -n '1,290p' src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj\"","aggregated_output":"#!/bin/sh\n# J7 UDP failure-injection probe runner, macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64. POSIX sh.\ndir=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\nif [ -z \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ] && [ -f build/tools/jolt-env.sh ]; then\n  . build/tools/jolt-env.sh\nfi\nif [ -z \"$JOLT\" ]; then\n  if [ -x build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt ]; then\n    JOLT=build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt\n  else\n    JOLT=build/jolt-spike/jolt/bin/jolt\n  fi\nfi\nif [ -z \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ]; then\n  mise_chez=\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\"\n  [ -x \"$mise_chez\" ] && JOLT_CHEZ=$mise_chez\nfi\n[ -n \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ] && export JOLT_CHEZ\n\n\"$JOLT\" -Srepro -M:jolt \"$dir/jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj\"\nrc=$?\necho \"exit: $rc\"\nexit $rc\n#!/bin/sh\n# J0b probe runner (foreground), macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64. POSIX sh\n# (Ubuntu's /bin/sh is dash). Run from the repository root.\n#\n#   JOLT       jolt binary. Default: build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt (J0a layout),\n#              else build/jolt-spike/jolt/bin/jolt (spike layout).\n#   JOLT_CHEZ  threaded Chez 10.x. Default: build/tools/jolt-env.sh's value when\n#              that file exists (J0a layout), else the mise 10.4.1 install path\n#              when present; otherwise left unset and jolt searches PATH.\ndir=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\nif [ -z \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ] && [ -f build/tools/jolt-env.sh ]; then\n  . build/tools/jolt-env.sh\nfi\nif [ -z \"$JOLT\" ]; then\n  if [ -x build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt ]; then\n    JOLT=build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt\n  else\n    JOLT=build/jolt-spike/jolt/bin/jolt\n  fi\nfi\nif [ -z \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ]; then\n  mise_chez=\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\"\n  [ -x \"$mise_chez\" ] && JOLT_CHEZ=$mise_chez\nfi\n[ -n \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ] && export JOLT_CHEZ\n\njolt_home=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$JOLT\")/..\" 2>/dev/null && pwd)\necho \"jolt: $JOLT\"\necho \"jolt-sha: $(git -C \"$jolt_home\" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null) dirty=$(git -C \"$jolt_home\" status --porcelain 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\"\nif [ -n \"$JOLT_CHEZ\" ]; then\n  echo \"chez: $JOLT_CHEZ $(\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" --version 2>&1)\"\nelse\n  echo \"chez: JOLT_CHEZ unset (jolt searches PATH)\"\nfi\n\ncase \"$(uname -s)\" in\n  Darwin)\n    echo \"uname: $(uname -sm) macOS $(sw_vers -productVersion 2>/dev/null)\"\n    echo \"sysctl: $(sysctl -n net.inet.udp.maxdgram net.inet.udp.recvspace kern.ipc.maxsockbuf 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')(maxdgram recvspace maxsockbuf)\"\n    echo \"lo0 mtu: $(ifconfig lo0 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/.*mtu \\([0-9]*\\).*/\\1/p' | head -1)\"\n    ;;\n  Linux)\n    os=$(sed -n 's/^PRETTY_NAME=\"\\(.*\\)\"$/\\1/p' /etc/os-release 2>/dev/null)\n    echo \"uname: $(uname -sm) $os\"\n    sys=\"\"\n    for k in core/wmem_default core/wmem_max core/rmem_default core/rmem_max ipv4/udp_wmem_min ipv4/udp_rmem_min ipv4/udp_mem; do\n      sys=\"$sys net.$(echo $k | tr / .)=$(tr '\\t' ' ' < /proc/sys/net/$k 2>/dev/null)\"\n    done\n    echo \"sysctl:$sys\"\n    echo \"lo mtu: $(cat /sys/class/net/lo/mtu 2>/dev/null)\"\n    ;;\n  *)\n    echo \"uname: $(uname -sm) (unsupported platform for this probe)\"\n    ;;\nesac\n\n\"$JOLT\" \"$dir/jolt_udp_probe.clj\"\nrc=$?\necho \"exit: $rc\"\nexit $rc\n;; J7 failure-injection probe: native UDP setup failure handling,\n;; exception and buffer cleanup, fatal error seam closure, and diagnostics.\n;; Run with:\n;;   bb probe:jolt-udp-failures\n(ns jolt-udp-failures-probe\n  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.datagram :as datagram]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [dao.stream.udp :as udp]\n            [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n            [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n            [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n\n(def pass-count (atom 0))\n(def fail-count (atom 0))\n\n(defn check [leg label condition data]\n  (if condition\n    (do\n      (swap! pass-count inc)\n      (println \"PASS\" leg label data))\n    (do\n      (swap! fail-count inc)\n      (println \"FAIL\" leg label data))))\n\n(defn traffic []\n  (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                                     ring/capacity-key 256})))\n\n(defn events [r]\n  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor r stream/anchor-oldest)) out []]\n    (let [v (stream/next r c)]\n      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome v))\n        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor v) (conj out (:dao.stream/value v)))\n        out))))\n\n(def closes (atom []))\n(def frees (atom []))\n\n(defn fake-host [f]\n  (reset! closes [])\n  (reset! frees [])\n  (with-redefs [native/c-socket (fn [& _] [123 0])\n                native/close-on-exec! (fn [_] true)\n                native/set-blocking! (fn [& _] [0 0])\n                native/set-int-option! (fn [& _] [0 0])\n                native/c-bind (fn [& _] [0 0])\n                native/local-address (fn [_] {:ip \"127.0.0.1\" :port 40001})\n                native/sockaddr-ip (fn [_] \"127.0.0.1\")\n                native/sockaddr-port (fn [_] 40002)\n                native/c-close (fn [fd] (swap! closes conj fd) [0 0])\n                poller/cancel! (fn [& _] nil)\n                poller/forget! (fn [& _] nil)]\n    (f)))\n\n(defn bind-seam [r & {:keys [bind-host bind-port] :or {bind-host \"127.0.0.1\" bind-port 0}}]\n  (udp/bind! {:identity \"probe-test\" :deposit r :bind-host bind-host :bind-port bind-port}))\n\n(def descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/datagram\n                 :dao.stream/identity \"probe-test\"\n                 :dao.stream.datagram/bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n                 :dao.stream.datagram/bind-port 40001})\n\n(def outbound {:dao.stream.datagram/destination\n               {:dao.stream.datagram/host \"127.0.0.1\" :dao.stream.datagram/port 40002}\n               :dao.stream.datagram/bytes \"BQY=\"})\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; 1. Setup Failures: close-on-exec! and IPV6_V6ONLY (Fix 1)\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (with-redefs [native/close-on-exec! (fn [_] false)]\n                 (bind-seam r))\n          evs (events r)]\n      (check 1 \"close-on-exec! failure closes acquired fd\"\n             (= [123] @closes)\n             {:closes @closes})\n      (check 1 \"close-on-exec! failure deposits bind-failed\"\n             (and (= 1 (count evs))\n                  (= :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed (:dao.stream.datagram/event (first evs)))\n                  (= \"close-on-exec! failed\" (:dao.stream.datagram/reason (first evs))))\n             {:events evs})\n      (check 1 \"close-on-exec! returns failed-seam (inert close and step)\"\n             (and (= {:progressed? false} ((:step! seam)))\n                  (nil? ((:close! seam))))\n             {}))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (with-redefs [native/set-int-option! (fn [& _] [-1 1])\n                             native/local-address (fn [_] {:ip \"::1\" :port 40001})]\n                 (bind-seam r :bind-host \"::1\"))\n          evs (events r)]\n      (check 1 \"IPV6_V6ONLY failure closes acquired fd\"\n             (= [123] @closes)\n             {:closes @closes})\n      (check 1 \"IPV6_V6ONLY failure deposits bind-failed with errno\"\n             (and (= 1 (count evs))\n                  (= :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed (:dao.stream.datagram/event (first evs)))\n                  (= \"IPV6_V6ONLY failed: errno 1\" (:dao.stream.datagram/reason (first evs))))\n             {:events evs})\n      (check 1 \"IPV6_V6ONLY failure returns failed-seam\"\n             (= {:progressed? false} ((:step! seam)))\n             {}))))\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; 2. Setup and Buffer Ownership Cleanup (Fix 2)\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (with-redefs [native/local-address (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"injected getsockname failure\" {})))]\n                 (bind-seam r))\n          evs (events r)]\n      (check 2 \"Setup exception closes acquired fd\"\n             (= [123] @closes)\n             {:closes @closes})\n      (check 2 \"Setup exception deposits bind-failed preserving original reason\"\n             (and (= 1 (count evs))\n                  (= :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed (:dao.stream.datagram/event (first evs)))\n                  (= \"injected getsockname failure\" (:dao.stream.datagram/reason (first evs))))\n             {:events evs})\n      (check 2 \"Setup exception returns failed-seam\"\n             (= {:progressed? false} ((:step! seam)))\n             {}))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          orig-ms native/make-sockaddr\n          seam (with-redefs [native/make-sockaddr\n                             (fn [fam ip port]\n                               (if (= port 40001)\n                                 (throw (ex-info \"injected make-sockaddr failure\" {}))\n                                 (orig-ms fam ip port)))]\n                 (bind-seam r :bind-port 40001))\n          evs (events r)]\n      (check 2 \"make-sockaddr bind failure closes acquired fd\"\n             (= [123] @closes)\n             {:closes @closes})\n      (check 2 \"make-sockaddr bind failure deposits bind-failed\"\n             (and (= 1 (count evs))\n                  (= \"injected make-sockaddr failure\" (:dao.stream.datagram/reason (first evs))))\n             {:events evs}))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    ;; Helper acquisition: make-sockaddr address-string allocation failure during bind\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          oa ffi/alloc\n          of ffi/free\n          ms native/make-sockaddr\n          live (atom {})\n          seam\n          (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n] (let [p (oa n)] (swap! live assoc p n) p))\n                        ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))\n                        native/make-sockaddr\n                        (fn [fam ip port]\n                          (if (= port 40001)\n                            (with-redefs [ffi/string->ptr (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"injected address string allocation failure\" {})))]\n                              (ms fam ip port))\n                            (ms fam ip port)))]\n            (udp/bind! {:identity \"partial-bind\" :deposit r :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\" :bind-port 40001}))\n          evs (events r)]\n      (check 2 \"Bind helper address-string failure leaves 0 unreleased bytes (no 16-byte leak)\"\n             (empty? @live)\n             {:unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live))})\n      (check 2 \"Bind helper address-string failure closes acquired fd\"\n             (= [123] @closes)\n             {:closes @closes})\n      (check 2 \"Bind helper address-string failure deposits bind-failed\"\n             (and (= 1 (count evs))\n                  (= :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed (:dao.stream.datagram/event (first evs)))\n                  (= \"injected address string allocation failure\" (:dao.stream.datagram/reason (first evs))))\n             {:events evs})\n      (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p)))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    ;; Helper acquisition: make-sockaddr address-string allocation failure during send\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (bind-seam r)\n          oa ffi/alloc\n          of ffi/free\n          ms native/make-sockaddr\n          live (atom {})]\n      (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n] (let [p (oa n)] (swap! live assoc p n) p))\n                    ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))\n                    native/make-sockaddr\n                    (fn [fam ip port]\n                      (if (= port 40002)\n                        (with-redefs [ffi/string->ptr (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"injected destination string allocation failure\" {})))]\n                          (ms fam ip port))\n                        (ms fam ip port)))]\n        (let [res (try ((:send! seam) \"127.0.0.1\" 40002 (byte-array 32))\n                       (catch Throwable t (ex-message t)))]\n          (check 2 \"Send helper address-string failure leaves 0 unreleased bytes (no buffer or sockaddr leak)\"\n                 (empty? @live)\n                 {:unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live)) :res res})\n          (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p)))))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    ;; Helper acquisition: alloc-sockaddr length-cell allocation failure during receive\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (bind-seam r)\n          oa ffi/alloc\n          of ffi/free\n          live (atom {})\n          result\n          (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n]\n                                    (if (= n 4)\n                                      (throw (ex-info \"injected socklen allocation failure\" {}))\n                                      (let [p (oa n)] (swap! live assoc p n) p)))\n                        ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))]\n            (try ((:step! seam)) (catch Throwable t (ex-message t))))]\n      (check 2 \"Receive helper length-cell failure leaves 0 unreleased bytes (no 128-byte leak)\"\n             (empty? @live)\n             {:unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live)) :result result})\n      (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p)))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    ;; Verify send-fn buffer cleanup when second allocation throws\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (bind-seam r)\n          orig-alloc ffi/alloc\n          orig-free ffi/free\n          orig-ms native/make-sockaddr\n          freed (atom [])]\n      (with-redefs [ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! freed conj p) (orig-free p))\n                    native/make-sockaddr (fn [fam ip port]\n                                           (if (= port 40002)\n                                             (throw (ex-info \"injected destination make-sockaddr error\" {}))\n                                             (orig-ms fam ip port)))]\n        (let [res (try ((:send! seam) \"127.0.0.1\" 40002 (byte-array 32))\n                       (catch Throwable t (ex-message t)))]\n          (check 2 \"send-fn frees payload buffer when destination sockaddr fails\"\n                 (pos? (count @freed))\n                 {:freed-count (count @freed) :res res}))))))\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    ;; Verify step-fn buffer cleanup when alloc-sockaddr throws\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (bind-seam r)\n          orig-free ffi/free\n          freed (atom [])]\n      (with-redefs [ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! freed conj p) (orig-free p))\n                    native/alloc-sockaddr (fn [] (throw (ex-info \"injected alloc-sockaddr error\" {})))]\n        (let [res (try ((:step! seam))\n                       (catch Throwable t (ex-message t)))]\n          (check 2 \"step-fn frees receive buffer when alloc-sockaddr throws\"\n                 (pos? (count @freed))\n                 {:freed-count (count @freed) :res res}))))))\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; 3. Fatal Descriptor Errors, Interruption and Diagnostics (Fix 3)\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(fake-host\n  (fn []\n    ;; Fatal error: ENOTSOCK (88)\n    (let [r (traffic)\n          seam (bind-seam r)\n          calls (atom 0)]\n      (binding [udp/*recvfrom* (fn [& _] (swap! calls inc) [-1 88])]\n        (let [turn1 ((:step! seam))\n              turn2 ((:step! seam))\n              turn3 ((:step! seam))\n              evs (events r)\n              diag (udp/diagnostics seam)]\n          (check 3 \"Fatal receive error returns not progressed\"\n                 (and (= {:progressed? false} turn1)\n                      (= {:progressed? false} turn2)\n                      (= {:progressed? false} turn3))\n                 {:turns [turn1 turn2 turn3]})\n          (check 3 \"Fatal receive error closes fd once\"\n                 (= [123] @closes)\n                 {:closes @closes})\n          (check 3 \"Fatal receive error deposits bound then closed\"\n                 (and (= 2 (count evs))\n                      (= :dao.stream.datagram/bound (:dao.stream.datagram/event (first evs)))\n                      (= :dao.stream.datagram/closed (:dao.stream.datagram/event (second evs))))\n                 {:events evs})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat .git; ls -ld .git build/tools/jolt; cat build/tools/jolt-env.sh; rg -n 'reopen|128 bytes|ECONNREFUSED|REOPENED|allocation|Confirmation' codex-confirm.stdout.log codex-confirm3.stdout.log collab/jolt/j7-fix.findings.md; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*injection*' -g '*confirm*' build/j7-review build/j7-review-confirm 2>/dev/null; command -v bb; command -v clojure; command -v mise; git diff 8668198f\"'^..ebbd0199 -- src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat .git; ls -ld .git build/tools/jolt; cat build/tools/jolt-env.sh; rg -n 'reopen|128 bytes|ECONNREFUSED|REOPENED|allocation|Confirmation' codex-confirm.stdout.log codex-confirm3.stdout.log collab/jolt/j7-fix.findings.md; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*injection*' -g '*confirm*' build/j7-review build/j7-review-confirm 2>/dev/null; command -v bb; command -v clojure; command -v mise; git diff 8668198f\"'^..ebbd0199 -- src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt'","aggregated_output":"gitdir: /home/sto/ci/datomworld-j6e-linux/.git/worktrees/dw-j7\n-rw-rw-r--  1 sto sto   63 Nov 15 15:08 .git\ndrwxrwxr-x 16 sto sto 4096 Oct 30 04:51 build/tools/jolt\n# written by bb bootstrap:jolt from jolt-toolchain.edn; do not edit\nexport JOLT_CHEZ='/home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme'\nexport JOLT_HOME='/home/sto/ci/dw-j7/build/tools/jolt'\nexport JOLT_PATCHES='/home/sto/ci/dw-j7/build/tools/jolt-patches.edn'\ncollab/jolt/j7-fix.findings.md:25:- **Issue**: Descriptor ownership was unprotected against throws after `c-socket` succeeded (e.g. `native/local-address` throw leaked descriptor and propagated unhandled exception). Send and receive temporary buffer allocations were also vulnerable to leaks if secondary allocations threw before `try` began.\ncodex-confirm.stdout.log:5:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short && git log -9 --oneline && git diff --stat fd195c0c..HEAD && cat collab/jolt/j7-review.findings.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"?? agy-fix.rc\\n?? agy-fix.stdout.log\\n?? agy-implement.rc\\n?? agy-implement.stdout.log\\n?? agy-implement2.rc\\n?? agy-implement2.stdout.log\\n?? agy-implement3.rc\\n?? agy-implement3.stdout.log\\n?? codex-architect.rc\\n?? codex-architect.stdout.log\\n?? codex-confirm.rc\\n?? codex-confirm.stdout.log\\n?? codex-review.rc\\n?? codex-review.stdout.log\\n?? codex-review2.rc\\n?? codex-review2.stdout.log\\n?? codex-review3.rc\\n?? codex-review3.stdout.log\\n?? collab/jolt/j7-review-confirm-prompt.md\\n336bc526 docs(collab): J7 fix round findings and acceptance evidence\\na7357c88 test(jolt): reconcile J7 applicability and add failure-injection probe (P1)\\n7d9346de fix(udp): retain receive diagnostics and close seam once on fatal descriptor errors (P2)\\n8f158fc5 fix(udp): establish immediate native buffer and descriptor cleanup on UDP paths (P2)\\nd6c76f5f fix(udp): check close-on-exec! and IPV6_V6ONLY results on native UDP bind (P2)\\nfd195c0c feat(dht): J7 slice 2 — DHT host composition on jolt and shell activation\\n16d4d3ed feat(udp): J7 slice 1 — native UDP datagram host seam and facade factoring\\n8ccfb897 docs(collab): the J7 architect design findings (codex gpt-6.1-sol round; committed by the orchestrator after the round left it untracked)\\n1ab4e9e6 docs(collab): the j7 review-round prompt\\n bb.edn                                         |   5 +\\n collab/jolt/j7-fix-prompt.md                   |  13 +\\n collab/jolt/j7-fix.findings.md                 | 225 +++++++++++++++\\n collab/jolt/j7-review.findings.md              | 178 ++++++++++++\\n src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj                       |  36 ++-\\n src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj            | 375 +++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.sh             |  24 ++\\n src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt                   | 330 +++++++++++++---------\\n test/resources/yin/repl/jolt-applicability.edn |  22 +-\\n 9 files changed, 1046 insertions(+), 162 deletions(-)\\nReviewed-GMT: 2026-11-16 03:58:16 UTC\\nReviewed-Local: 2026-11-15 22:58:16 EST\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\nRole: reviewer\\nBranch: `fix/j7-udp-dht`\\nReviewed-HEAD: `fd195c0cf0c7a62cd21915b8bcde3cb3e2231509`\\nReviewed-base: `origin/master` = `d972c2c4349f807d1ddd67d7a6741d09ee69d611`\\nVerdict: request changes; J7 acceptance incomplete. Four actionable findings; no implementation fixes made.\\n\\n# Findings\\n\\nP1 | src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:252 | Jolt DHT activation lands without the J7 production-seam and composition acceptance required by §8.4 and the committed design §§6–7. The diff adds no tests, no jolt process roles, and no applicability reconciliation. The retained J0b probe exercises its own syscalls, while the claimed solo smoke explicitly opens no socket. | Add and run production IPv4/IPv6, configurable-size, failure/cleanup and DHT/signed-board process tests; reconcile the J7 exclusions and supply the required host/interoperability evidence before accepting J7 as complete.\\n\\nP2 | src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt:155 | Socket setup ignores the boolean result of `native/close-on-exec!` and the `[result errno]` from `IPV6_V6ONLY` at line 162. Injecting either failure still deposits `bound` and retains the socket. Failed close-on-exec can leak a duplicate into children and keep a port alive after owner close; failed IPv6-only setup can admit mapped IPv4 ingress where the design requires a deterministic single-family seam. | Check both results, close the acquired descriptor, and deposit `bind-failed` with the actual failure instead of exposing a partially configured seam.\\n\\nP2 | src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt:151 | Descriptor ownership is not protected against exceptions after `socket()` succeeds. Injecting a throw from `native/local-address` propagates the exception, deposits no `bind-failed`, and calls close zero times. Earlier setup helpers can also throw; the per-buffer send/receive `try` blocks likewise start after a second native acquisition at lines 199 and 235. | Establish cleanup immediately after each acquisition; on failed bind release the descriptor and native allocations and report `bind-failed`, preserving the original reason. Apply the same ownership discipline to send/receive temporary buffers.\\n\\nP2 | src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt:244 | Every negative receive result loses its errno and diagnostic; only `EBADF` closes the seam. With Linux `ENOTSOCK` (88) injected, three owner turns issue three receives, each answering only `{:progressed? false}`, with no closure or error observation. A permanently broken seam therefore looks idle and is retried indefinitely by the owner. | Retain explicit instance-owned receive diagnostics, including errno, and close fatal descriptor errors once; leave interruption recoverable and would-block silent, without adding a public lifecycle kind or retrying inside a turn.\\n\\n## Evidence and scope\\n\\nThe review inspected every changed source file and the complete committed\\n[architect findings](1794773141000-architect-j7-design.findings.md),\\n[engineer report](1794775739000-engineer-j7-impl.findings.md),\\n[§8.4 and J7 gate](../../docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md), and\\n[datagram contract](../../docs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md).\\nImplementation commits: `16d4d3ed` and `fd195c0c`. The engineer identifies\\nthe work as slices 1 and 2; this review does not reinterpret that as evidence\\nthat the remaining design gates passed.\\n\\nFor finding 1, `git diff --name-only origin/master..HEAD` contains seven source\\nfiles and three collaboration documents, with no test or runner changes.\\n`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:182–218` still excludes UDP, DHT, head-board and\\nhead-follow namespaces. `test/resources/yin/repl/jolt-applicability.edn:6–29`\\nretains J7 per-test exclusions whose reasons cite the now-removed refusal.\\nCodec-neutral board fixtures still require Transit\\n(`test/yin/vm/linker/head_board_test.cljc:27`). There is no native UDP test\\naddition, jolt role in `test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj`, or macOS and\\nJVM/Node/Dart interoperation result in the engineer report. Passing portable\\ntests below cannot fill these gaps.\\n\\nFor findings 2–4, the review-only script in ignored\\n`build/j7-review/native-injection.clj` invokes the actual production binder,\\nclosures, public datagram writer, address encoding and traffic rings. Socket\\ncreation/bind/flags/local-address/close and poller cleanup are replaced with\\ncontrolled functions; the fake fd is 123. This avoids the sandbox's socket\\nrestriction and does not claim a real socket was opened. Observations:\\n\\n```text\\nclose-on-exec! -> false:\\n  events = [bound at 127.0.0.1:40001]; closes-before-close = []\\nIPv6 set-int-option! -> [-1 1]:\\n  events = [bound at ::1:40001]; closes-before-close = []\\nlocal-address -> throws \\\"injected getsockname failure\\\":\\n  result = propagated exception; events = []; closes = []\\nrecvfrom -> [-1 88], on three successive turns:\\n  turns = [{:progressed? false} {:progressed? false} {:progressed? false}]\\n  calls = 3; events = [bound]; closes-before-close = []\\n```\\n\\nThe exception reproducer tests setup ownership, not whether the C\\n`getsockname` syscall itself throws. `native/local-address` allocates native\\nsockaddr storage; exceptions from this or other fallible helper work must\\nstill release the descriptor. In send/receive, failure of the second\\nallocation occurs before the first buffer's release has been protected.\\nThose additional allocation sites were inspected, not separately injected.\\n\\n# Independently executed acceptance\\n\\nHost: Linux x86_64, Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS. Runtime: clean jolt\\n`b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3`; Chez 10.4.1, matching the declared\\npin. The existing bootstrap environment was used; bootstrap was not rerun.\\nEvery result below is from a fresh review command; actual output was read.\\nAn earlier untracked review was present at the requested output path. Its\\nsource claims and review-only injection script were inspected and all eight\\nchecks below were independently rerun in this turn; the old report and logs\\nwere not used as acceptance results. The inspected injection script remains\\nin ignored `build/j7-review/`; fresh command outputs were read directly from\\nthe execution tool.\\n\\nShell setup for `bb`/JVM commands:\\n\\n```sh\\nexport MISE_STATE_DIR=\\\"$PWD/build/j7-review/mise-state\\\"\\nexport MISE_CACHE_DIR=\\\"$PWD/build/j7-review/mise-cache\\\"\\neval \\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\"\\n```\\n\\nJolt commands first source `. build/tools/jolt-env.sh`. Timeout wrappers\\nbounded the namespace load at 60 seconds and other checks at 120 seconds;\\nnone of the reported successful checks timed out.\\n\\n| Check | Command | Actual result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Jolt namespace loads | `\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt -e \\\"(require 'dao.stream.udp 'dao.stream.udp.common 'dao.posix.random 'dao.space.dht 'yin.shell.dht 'yin.repl) (println :j7-all-namespaces-loaded-ok)\\\"` | Exit 0; `:j7-all-namespaces-loaded-ok`. |\\n| J0b retained legs | `bb probe:jolt-udp` | Exit 1 before the first assertion: `Unhandled exception: socket failed`, `ex-data: {:errno 1}`, at `jolt-udp-probe/udp-open` line 76. Header confirms the clean pinned SHA. No leg passed here. |\\n| Solo DHT smoke | `printf '(+ 1 2)\\\\n' \\\\| \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-yin-repl --no-state --index-store dht:/tmp/j7-review4-solo-20261115` | Exit 0; `yin> 3`, nine durable local blobs, explicit solo/no-socket/no-ack message, `Bye`. |\\n| JVM load | `clojure -M -e \\\"(require 'yin.shell.dht 'yin.repl) (println :jvm-load-ok)\\\"` | Exit 0; `:jvm-load-ok`. |\\n| Claimed JVM UDP/datagram suites | `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.udp-test -n dao.stream.udp-raw-test -n dao.stream.datagram-test` | Exit 0; 37 tests, 185 assertions, 0 failures/errors. |\\n| Same portable suites on jolt | `\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.stream.udp-test dao.stream.udp-raw-test dao.stream.datagram-test` | Exit 0; 37 tests, 185 assertions, 0 failures/errors/load failures. |\\n| Signed-head and mesh follower on jolt | `\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj yin.vm.linker.head-test yin.vm.linker.head-follow-test` | Exit 0; 32 tests, 920 assertions, 0 failures/errors/load failures. Portable test mesh, not native UDP/WS processes. |\\n| Production seam injection | `\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt build/j7-review/native-injection.clj` | Exit 0; 35 contract assertions passed, plus the adverse setup/receive observations quoted above. |\\n\\nThe smoke adds `--no-state` and uses a fresh directory so it does not write\\nthe user's saved `~/.yin/node/state.edn` or reuse the implementer's store.\\nIt preserves the requested evaluation and DHT store behavior. Its output:\\n\\n```text\\ndht: solo, no --dht-peer, so no socket is opened; publications are durable in /tmp/j7-review4-solo-20261115 and acknowledged by no one\\nyin> 3\\nyin> dht: published :segment/blake3-3ecb092cc91ce58deabf9d9c3dd3f129b7371de9c6396926400f173022dfd09b (9 blobs), NOT acknowledged: solo: no --dht-peer is configured, so nothing was sent; the index is in /tmp/j7-review4-solo-20261115 only; 9 of 9 blobs not sent; not retrying (every remaining failure is final); the local copy is durable\\nBye\\n```\\n\\nThe J0b failure is an environment limitation, not an implementation defect\\nor evidence against the implementer's historical 37-pass run. This review\\ncannot independently confirm that run: `socket()` is denied with EPERM here.\\nThe wrapper also reports absent `/proc/sys/net/ipv4/udp_mem`; that diagnostic\\nis separate from the socket failure. No sandbox bypass or alternate runtime\\nwas used. Real native IPv4/IPv6, readiness/fiber legs and macOS acceptance\\nremain unverified.\\n\\n## Contract and portability disposition\\n\\nThe injected production writer cases EAGAIN, ENOBUFS, EMSGSIZE, EINTR and\\nshort-send each returned `transport-error` and exactly one `send-failed`,\\nmade one send call, and made no later send during two receive turns. None\\nreturned `full`. Closed sends returned `closed`; closed stepping was inert.\\nAn oversize sentinel consumed the full 64-call receive budget without\\ndepositing a packet; would-block returned immediately; repeated close closed\\nonce. Inspection confirms no outbound queue, send-side wait, EINTR retry or\\nPOLLOUT replay. Actual nonblocking flags and packet/source fidelity still\\nneed real socket acceptance. Receive diagnostic handling fails as reported.\\n\\nThe shared UDP body moved without wire-key or algorithm changes; its public\\nfunctions/arities and `dao.stream.udp.UdpHandle` facade remain available.\\nBoth JVM and jolt portable suites pass. No top-level conditional `require`\\nwas introduced. Jolt imports remain within `.jolt` files and the existing\\nnamespace reader-conditional seam in `dao.space.dht`; shared\\n`udp/common.cljc` remains portable. Entropy lowering retains the qualified\\n`dao.host.hash` provenance gate; `dao.space` does not depend on `yin.*`.\\nThe optional native receive turn precedes DHT interpretation as designed.\\n\\nJVM binder/entropy selection retains its original reader branch. Shared\\nfacade factoring and shell-board CBOR dialing do affect JVM-loaded source;\\nthe latter is explicitly required by design §4, with CBOR first and Transit\\nretained on supporting listeners. JVM load and affected UDP tests passed;\\nthat does not qualify board negotiation, Node/Dart compilation or process\\ninteroperability. Those remain open, rather than establishing that the JVM\\nlane is wholly unchanged or broken.\\n\\nOnly this findings artifact is intended for the requested commit. No source,\\ntest, applicability file or supplied execution log was changed or staged.\\nThe existing review script, backups and logs are ignored build output.\\n`git diff --check origin/master..HEAD` passed.\\n\\n## Commit status\\n\\nFindings whitespace validation passed. The findings-only commit command was\\nattempted:\\n\\n```sh\\ngit add -- collab/jolt/j7-review.findings.md &&\\ngit commit -m \\\"docs(collab): independent J7 implementation review findings\\\" -- collab/jolt/j7-review.findings.md\\n```\\n\\n`git add` exited 128 before staging, so the commit did not run:\\n\\n```text\\nfatal: Unable to create '/home/sto/ci/datomworld-j6e-linux/.git/worktrees/dw-j7/index.lock': Read-only file system\\n```\\n\\nThe linked worktree's Git metadata is outside the session's writable roots.\\nThe completed report remains untracked at the requested path; no commit was\\ncreated. Completing the commit requires an environment permitted to write\\nthat metadata. No Git metadata or permissions were changed to bypass the\\nrestriction. The earlier untracked report was preserved in ignored\\n`build/j7-review/review-before-refresh-20261116.findings.md`.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncodex-confirm.stdout.log:9:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat collab/jolt/j7-fix.findings.md && git diff fd195c0c..HEAD -- src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj test/resources/yin/repl/jolt-applicability.edn bb.edn && cat src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.sh'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-16 04:20:00 UTC\\nCoding-Agent: agy\\nRole: engineer\\nBranch: `fix/j7-udp-dht`\\nBase: `fd195c0cf0c7a62cd21915b8bcde3cb3e2231509`\\nTask: J7 fix round — the review findings P1-P2x3\\n\\n# J7 Fix Findings and Acceptance Report\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nAddresses and resolves all four review findings from [`collab/jolt/j7-review.findings.md`](j7-review.findings.md) (verdict: request changes), maintaining full integrity of landed Slices 1 and 2, adding regression failure-injection coverage, and reconciling test applicability without falsely claiming full J7 process gate completion.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Addressed Findings\\n\\n### 1. P2 (udp.jolt:155,162): Check close-on-exec! boolean and IPV6_V6ONLY [result errno]\\n- **Issue**: Socket setup ignored the boolean return of `native/close-on-exec!` and the `[result errno]` return from `IPV6_V6ONLY` `native/set-int-option!`. Injecting failures deposited `bound` and retained the socket.\\n- **Fix**:\\n  - `(if-not (native/close-on-exec! fd) ...)`: on `false`, closes acquired descriptor and deposits `:dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed` with `\\\"close-on-exec! failed\\\"`, returning `failed-seam`.\\n  - For IPv6 binds, checks `[r-v6 err-v6] (native/set-int-option! fd native/ipproto-ipv6 native/ipv6-v6only 1)`: on `(neg? r-v6)`, closes descriptor and deposits `:dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed` with `(str \\\"IPV6_V6ONLY failed: errno \\\" err-v6)`, returning `failed-seam`.\\n\\n### 2. P2 (udp.jolt:151 + 199,235): Immediate descriptor & buffer cleanup on native acquisition\\n- **Issue**: Descriptor ownership was unprotected against throws after `c-socket` succeeded (e.g. `native/local-address` throw leaked descriptor and propagated unhandled exception). Send and receive temporary buffer allocations were also vulnerable to leaks if secondary allocations threw before `try` began.\\n- **Fix**:\\n  - Immediately following non-negative `fd` acquisition from `native/c-socket`, establishes `close-fd!` and executes all subsequent setup within `try ... (catch Throwable t (close-fd!) (failed-seam deposit identity (or (ex-message t) (str t))))`. On any setup throw, `fd` is closed, native storage freed, and `bind-failed` deposited preserving the original reason.\\n  - In `send-fn`, `(ffi/alloc (max 1 len))` is immediately protected by `try ... (finally (ffi/free buf))` before `(native/make-sockaddr ...)` is called.\\n  - In `step-fn`, `(ffi/alloc cap)` is immediately protected by `try ... (finally (ffi/free buf))` before `(native/alloc-sockaddr)` is called.\\n\\n### 3. P2 (udp.jolt:244): Retain receive diagnostics; close seam once on fatal descriptor errors\\n- **Issue**: Negative receive results lost their errno and diagnostics; only `EBADF` closed the seam. Injecting `ENOTSOCK` (88) caused owner turns to retry indefinitely without error observation.\\n- **Fix**:\\n  - Added instance-owned `diagnostics` atom on every seam instance, accessible via `:diagnostics`, `:diagnostic`, and helper `(dao.stream.udp/diagnostics seam)`.\\n  - **Fatal descriptor errors** (any negative receive result other than would-block and EINTR, e.g. `ENOTSOCK`, `EBADF`, `EINVAL`): records `{:kind :fatal-descriptor-error :errno e :reason (str \\\"recvfrom fatal error: errno \\\" e)}` in diagnostics, calls `close-fn` once (canceling/forgetting poller, closing fd, depositing `closed` event, and setting `@closed? true`), and finishes turn immediately without retrying. Subsequent owner calls to `step!` return `{:progressed? false}` immediately without issuing syscalls. Subsequent `close!` calls are idempotent.\\n  - **Interruption** (`EINTR` 4): stays recoverable; records `{:kind :interrupted :errno 4 :reason \\\"recvfrom interrupted: errno 4\\\"}` in diagnostics, does not close socket, does not retry inside the turn, and leaves the descriptor open and usable for subsequent turns.\\n  - **Would-block** (`EAGAIN` 11, `ENOBUFS` 105): stays silent; finishes turn immediately without closing descriptor or recording error diagnostics.\\n\\n### 4. P1 (acceptance reconciliation): Applicability updates and failure-injection probe\\n- **Reconciliation**:\\n  - Updated 11 stale test exclusions in `test/resources/yin/repl/jolt-applicability.edn` that cited the removed J7 refusal. Each now cites the landed state: `J7 slice 1+2 landed; networked DHT peer/follow acceptance open per design §§6-7`.\\n  - Updated 14 stale test namespace exclusions in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` to cite landed Slices 1 and 2, and explicitly document why each remains excluded per design §§6–7 (multi-process DHT roles, real socket fixtures, Transit requirements on board fixtures, cross-host interop).\\n  - Explicitly did **NOT** claim full J7 gate completion: design §§6–7 process/interop acceptance remains open and recorded.\\n- **Failure-Injection Regression Probe (`bb probe:jolt-udp-failures`)**:\\n  - Added `probe:jolt-udp-failures` in `bb.edn` backed by `src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.sh` and `src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj`.\\n  - Exercises 68 assertions across setup failures, throw cleanup, buffer ownership, fatal error seam closure, recoverable EINTR, silent would-block, and complete production writer/seam contracts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Independently Executed Acceptance Evidence\\n\\nAll commands run on Linux x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS, clean jolt `b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3`, Chez 10.4.1.\\n\\n### 1. J0b UDP Probe (retained baseline)\\n```sh\\nbb probe:jolt-udp\\n```\\n**Output**:\\n```text\\njolt: build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt\\njolt-sha: b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3 dirty=0\\nchez: /home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme 10.4.1\\nuname: Linux x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS\\nsysctl: net.core.wmem_default=212992 net.core.wmem_max=4194304 net.core.rmem_default=212992 net.core.rmem_max=4194304 net.ipv4.udp_wmem_min=4096 net.ipv4.udp_rmem_min=4096 net.ipv4.udp_mem=1533171 2044230 3066342\\nlo mtu: 65536\\njolt: source mode; run 'make devboot' to precompile\\njolt UDP probe, platform= :linux os.name= Linux os.arch= amd64 constants= {:sock-dgram 2, :ipproto-udp 17, :so-sndbuf 7, :so-rcvbuf 8, :msg-trunc 32, :eagain 11, :emsgsize 90, :enobufs 105, :ebadf 9}\\nPASS 2 above platform max: sendto fails EMSGSIZE (an error, nothing sent) {:so-sndbuf 212992, :so-rcvbuf 212992, :max-sendable 65507, :send-max+1 {:result :emsgsize, :errno 90}}\\nplatform max sendable = 65507 configured larger N = 8192\\nPASS 2 configured larger N is below the observed platform send maximum {:N 1200, :larger-N 8192, :max-sendable 65507}\\nPASS 1 bound ports read back {:a {:family 2, :ip \\\"127.0.0.1\\\", :port 57993, :scope-id 0}, :b {:family 2, :ip \\\"127.0.0.1\\\", :port 34950, :scope-id 0}}\\nPASS 1 empty socket answers :would-block {:result :would-block, :errno 11}\\nPASS 1 zero-length round-trip {:len 0, :send {:result :sent, :n 0}, :recv {:result :packet, :from {:ip \\\"127.0.0.1\\\", :port 57993}, :waits 0}, :recv-len 0}\\nPASS 1 embedde