es from the open process and interoperability gate. This session is read-only, so I can review and run compatible checks, but can’t write or commit the confirmation file.\n\nThe binder now checks close-on-exec and IPv6-only setup, protects more allocations with cleanup, and records receive errors. I’m checking two remaining edge cases: a failure inside a helper that allocates multiple buffers, and a packet-delivery error being treated as a fatal socket error.\n\n/bin/bash -lc '. build/tools/jolt-env.sh && timeout 120 \"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt -e \"$(cat <<'\"'CLJ'\n(load-file \\\"build/j7-review/native-injection.clj\\\")\n(fake-host\n (fn []\n   (let [r (traffic) seam (bind-seam r) oa ffi/alloc of ffi/free live (atom {})\n         result\n         (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n]\n                                  (if (= n 4)\n                                    (throw (ex-info \\\"injected socklen allocation failure\\\" {}))\n                                    (let [p (oa n)] (swap\"'! live assoc p n) p)))\n                       ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))]\n           (try ((:step! seam)) (catch Throwable t (ex-message t))))]\n     (println :partial-recv-acquisition :result result :unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live)))\n     (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p))\n     ((:close! seam)))))\n(fake-host\n (fn []\n   (let [r (traffic) oa ffi/alloc of ffi/free ms native/make-sockaddr live (atom {})\n         result\n         (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n] (let [p (oa n)] (swap! live assoc p n) p))\n                       ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))\n                       native/make-sockaddr\n                       (fn [fam ip port]\n                         (if (= port 40001)\n                           (with-redefs [ffi/string->ptr (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"injected address string allocation failure\" {})))]\n                             (ms fam ip port))\n                           (ms fam ip port)))]\n           (udp/bind! {:identity \"partial-bind\" :deposit r :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\" :bind-port 40001}))]\n     (println :partial-bind-acquisition :events (events r) :closes @closes :unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live)))\n     (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p))\n     ((:close! result)))))\n(fake-host\n (fn []\n   (let [r (traffic) seam (bind-seam r) calls (atom 0)]\n     (binding [udp/*recvfrom* (fn [& _] (swap! calls inc) (if (= 1 @calls) [-1 111] [-1 udp/EAGAIN]))]\n       (println :recv-econnrefused :turn1 ((:step! seam)) :turn2 ((:step! seam))\n                :calls @calls :closes @closes :diagnostics (udp/diagnostics seam)\n                :next-send ((:send! seam) \"127.0.0.1\" 40002 (byte-array 0))))\n     ((:close! seam)))))\nCLJ\n)\"'\n/bin/bash -lc '. build/tools/jolt-env.sh && timeout 120 \"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt -e \"$(cat <<'\"'CLJ'\n(load-file \\\"build/j7-review/native-injection.clj\\\")\n(fake-host\n (fn []\n   (let [r (traffic) seam (bind-seam r) oa ffi/alloc of ffi/free live (atom {})\n         result\n         (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n]\n                                  (if (= n 4)\n                                    (throw (ex-info \\\"injected socklen allocation failure\\\" {}))\n                                    (let [p (oa n)] (swap\"'! live assoc p n) p)))\n                       ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))]\n           (try ((:step! seam)) (catch Throwable t (ex-message t))))]\n     (println :partial-recv-acquisition :result result :unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live)))\n     (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p))\n     ((:close! seam)))))\n(fake-host\n (fn []\n   (let [r (traffic) oa ffi/alloc of ffi/free ms native/make-sockaddr live (atom {})\n         result\n         (with-redefs [ffi/alloc (fn [n] (let [p (oa n)] (swap! live assoc p n) p))\n                       ffi/free (fn [p] (swap! live dissoc p) (of p))\n                       native/make-sockaddr\n                       (fn [fam ip port]\n                         (if (= port 40001)\n                           (with-redefs [ffi/string->ptr (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"injected address string allocation failure\" {})))]\n                             (ms fam ip port))\n                           (ms fam ip port)))]\n           (udp/bind! {:identity \"partial-bind\" :deposit r :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\" :bind-port 40001}))]\n     (println :partial-bind-acquisition :events (events r) :closes @closes :unreleased-sizes (vec (vals @live)))\n     (doseq [p (keys @live)] (of p))\n     ((:close! result)))))\n(fake-host\n (fn []\n   (let [r (traffic) seam (bind-seam r) calls (atom 0)]\n     (binding [udp/*recvfrom* (fn [& _] (swap! calls inc) (if (= 1 @calls) [-1 111] [-1 udp/EAGAIN]))]\n       (println :recv-econnrefused :turn1 ((:step! seam)) :turn2 ((:step! seam))\n                :calls @calls :closes @closes :diagnostics (udp/diagnostics seam)\n                :next-send ((:send! seam) \"127.0.0.1\" 40002 (byte-array 0))))\n     ((:close! seam)))))\nCLJ\n)\"'\nThe new probe passes 68/68, and the original injection script now confirms both setup-option failures close the fd and report `bind-failed`; ENOTSOCK closes only once.\n\nTwo edge cases still fail: partial helper allocation leaves native memory unreleased, and an injected ECONNREFUSED permanently closes the seam. I’ll reopen those two P2 findings. J0b remains blocked by EPERM, and the solo smoke cannot create its store under this session’s read-only policy.\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-16 04:33:24 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-15 23:33:24 EST\n\n**Request changes.** Reviewed HEAD `336bc526`.\n\n- **P1 | ACCEPTED OPEN** — Applicability wording and the new probe address the authorized partial scope. Full process/interop acceptance remains open.\n- **P2 | FIXED AND VERIFIED** — [Socket-option checks](/home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt:174) now close once and deposit `bind-failed` for close-on-exec and V6ONLY failures.\n- **P2 | REOPEN: acquisition cleanup** — Outer cleanup works, but [helper acquisitions](/home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt:269) still leak on partial failure. Injecting failure in the receive helper’s length-cell allocation leaves **128 bytes** unreleased; failing address-string allocation during bind leaves **16 bytes**. Make the helpers exception-safe and test each acquisition.\n- **P2 | REOPEN: receive-error classification** — ENOTSOCK close-once and EINTR recovery pass, but the [catch-all fatal branch](/home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt:291) permanently closes the seam on injected ECONNREFUSED (111). Subsequent sends return `closed`. Linux UDP can report asynchronous errors from earlier packets; distinguish those from fatal descriptor errors. [Linux udp(7)](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/udp.7.html)\n\nVerified outputs: new probe **68/68**, original injection script **35 assertions passed**, namespace loads passed, JVM load passed, and JVM/jolt portable suites each passed **37 tests / 185 assertions**. JVM checks used existing cached classpaths because the CLI could not write its cache.\n\nJ0b stopped before assertions with socket EPERM. The solo smoke failed to create its directory under the read-only policy; neither counts as a pass.\n\n**The read-only session prevented creating `collab/jolt/j7-review-confirm.findings.md` or committing it.** No implementation changes were made.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
